From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:27:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: KK_MSL_OPT bits 256 (one math_mode block per run
 of statements) and 512 (coherent per address base)

256: consecutive ALU statements with the same math mode share one
'{ #pragma METAL fp math_mode }' block (register reads/writes may sit inside
a run). Megakernel p020: 9,628 -> 1,911 blocks, MSL -23 %.

512: msl_nir_mark_unwritten_loads traces every device address to the values
its pointer bits come from and marks loads whose bases no store or atomic
of the shader uses; KK_WORKAROUND_6 leaves those non-coherent. One buffer
bound through two descriptors counts as two bases. Runs as the last SSA
pass so the mark cannot make an earlier pass move a guarded load.

Both opt-in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
